15. Acceptance checks

Penn/Berkeley selections, search, filters and selected company persist across Globe, Network and Table. Back restores navigation state.

A multi-campus venture counts once in All campuses and appears appropriately in each supported campus view.

Campus markers cannot be mistaken for company HQ; unknown locations remain discoverable.

Source counts distinguish people, projects, ventures and portfolio references. Unscanned campus is not displayed as a verified zero.

Every visible graph edge can reveal evidence. Missing relationships are not manufactured to make the graph attractive.

A record with only an award can appear in Needs research without a fabricated product description or numerical assessment.

Researching a company adds supported evidence, preserves notes, and updates relevant views without duplicate entities or false completed states.

An empty shortlist offers the appropriate next action. Failed scans retain last successful results and show a real error state.

Opening a company, saving it, adding it to pipeline and returning to results works by mouse and keyboard.

At 1440px, 1024px and 390px widths: readable company information, no page-level horizontal overflow, accessible controls and no clipped drawer actions. Intentional table scrolling is contained.

Reduced motion and WebGL failure still allow the full research workflow.

Capture before/after screenshots of Explore, selected-company drawer, Network, Globe and Sources. Report checks actually performed and any unavailable modes.

16. Paste into Claude Code

Read UNIVERSITY_SOURCES_SHORTLIST.md and this UIUX_UPGRADE_CLAUDE.md alongside the existing project instructions. Improve the existing app in place. Prioritize Penn and Berkeley sourcing, clear company/founder research, and synchronized Globe/Network/Table exploration. Use the explicit layout and behavior above, preserve existing records and scoring rules, and complete the critical workflows. Do not stop at a visual mockup or populate screens with fake data. Return the implemented changes, actual source-run results, verification performed and specific unresolved blockers.